    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1229">

                <pb facs="1208" n="1042" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1042"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/362</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Parker,
                        representing American interests, to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-13T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1917, 12
                        noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>675. Department’s 661, February 12, 4 p.m. Minister Fomento Morry informed me
                    that he had taken up with General Carranza the matter of declaring forfeited the
                    properties of such persons as have not complied with decree or asked for
                    extension. He pointed out that five months have elapsed since the issuance of
                    the decree and that he considered that this was sufficient time for interested
                    parties to have shown cause for nonoperation. I do not think decree will be
                    withdrawn but my impression is that no drastic action will be taken although I
                    have nothing official on which to base my opinion. Have again taken matter up
                    with Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
